From d3a0973ae7b9de0f97964f414ff1f644e8c69aaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:45:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/65] CUDA/HIP: RDNA3 verify batches of 9-16 columns: WMMA
 small-N MUL_MAT kernel, wide MMVQ dispatch

mul_mat_vec_q_wmma (gfx110x): a wave computes 16 weight rows x 16 src1 columns with
v_wmma_i32_16x16x16_iu8 on the q8_1 activations of the MMVQ path (each lane holds one half of a 32-value
sub-block, the second WMMA uses the v_permlanex16-swapped halves), scales per sub-block in float (q8_1
scales via ds_bpermute), K split over 8 waves per block. Types: Q4_K, Q5_K, Q6_K, IQ4_XS, Q3_K, Q8_0,
IQ4_NL; bias (residual) epilogue, pair launch and channel/sample broadcast as the MMVQ kernel. Used from
9 columns (Q6_K from 7). The other multi-column types keep the dp4a kernel up to 10 columns, the rest MMQ.
GDN alpha/beta kernel and the q4_0-KV FlashAttention kernel accept up to 16 tokens.

Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL verify forward (llama-bench -d 2048, q4_0 KV): 9 columns 49.2 -> 32.1 ms,
16 columns 51.0 -> 35.0 ms; Uncensored Q4_K_M 53.7 -> 29.8 / 55.5 -> 33.1 ms; n <= 8 unchanged.
KLD vs b512 (ub 7/9/12/16): 0.0122/0.0128/0.0127/0.0127, base ub 6: 0.0124 +- 0.0006.
